 upernatural\n\nA multimedia presentation of Japanese art and live jazz by 
 the Fumi Tomita Quartet.\n\n  Fumi Tomita\, bass\n  Carl Clements\, woodwi
 nds\n  Jason Ennis\, guitars\n  Gary Fieldman\, drums\n\nFumi Tomita is a 
 jazz bassist\, composer\, educator\, and author.  His newest recording\, Y
 okai! Songs of the Japanese Supernatural will be released in October 2026 
 on Origin records and was inspired by 19th-century woodblock prints of Yok
 ai and other Japanese supernatural creatures derived from folklore.  The a
 lbum will be supported by a Northeast tour during October and November.  H
 is 2019 recording\, The Elephant Vanishes: Jazz Interpretations of the Sho
 rt Stories of Haruki Murakami\, was released to critical acclaim by Origin
  Arts records and was listed in the top ten records of 2019 by Jazziz. His
  2020 release Celebrating Bird: The Music of Charlie Parker was similarly 
 received.   \n\nTomita was active on the New York city jazz scene for over
  fifteen years and has performed at venues all over the U.S. and Canada in
 cluding recent appearances at the International Society of Bassists Confer
 ence in Ann Harbor\, Michigan in June 2023 and the Jazz Education Network 
 conference in New Orleans and a short tour of Georgia\, both in January 20
 24.\n\nAs an author\, his second book\, Introduction to Early Jazz: A Conc
 ise Introduction from Its Beginnings through 1929\, was published by State
  University of New York Press in February 2024 and was a guest on The Buzz
